1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,670
We know it’s good to learn another language.
我们都知道学习另一门语言有很多好处。

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:10,940
It opens doors, makes you more employable, helps you make new friends, and it’s fun too.
它能为你打开机遇之门，让你更具就业竞争力，帮助你结交新朋友，而且学习过程本身也充满乐趣。

3
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:21,110
But to improve our linguistic skills, many of us have to endure hours of school lessons or evening classes, with our heads buried in textbooks.
但为了提升语言技能，我们很多人不得不忍受很久的课堂教学或夜校课程，埋头于课本之中。

4
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:28,070
It’s no wonder then that technology appears to be providing a better and more accessible way of learning.
因此，技术似乎能够提供一种更好、更便捷的学习方式，也就不足为奇了。

5
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:37,540
There is certainly a huge demand for language learning, and having a smartphone means you can have a virtual teacher with you wherever you go.
语言学习的需求无疑非常巨大，而拥有智能手机意味着你无论走到哪里，都能拥有一位虚拟老师。

6
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:49,120
Many app developers are keen to cash in on the demand, and there are numerous learning apps available – including our own, free, BBC Learning English app!
许多应用程序开发者都急于抓住这一需求商机，市面上涌现出了大量学习类应用——包括我们免费的BBC英语学习应用！

7
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:58,040
One of many popular apps, Duolingo, offers 91 courses in 30 languages and has more than 300 million users.
多邻国（Duolingo）就是其中一款热门应用，它提供30种语言的91门课程，用户数量已超过3亿。

8
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:06,630
Some educational apps offer languages not popular enough to be taught at evening classes, or at most universities.
一些教育类应用会提供那些不够热门、无法在夜校或大多数大学里学到的语言课程。

9
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:17,680
And others offer ‘invented’ language courses in Esperanto, Elvish and Star Trek's Klingon – lessons you might not find in a traditional classroom.
还有一些应用提供世界语、精灵语、《星际迷航》中的克林贡语等“人造语言”课程——这些课程在传统课堂上你可能根本找不到。

10
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:25,520
Whatever you want to learn, apps allow you to go at your own pace and fit learning around other commitments.
无论你想学什么，应用程序都能让你按照自己的节奏学习，并能在其他事务中灵活安排学习时间。

11
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:35,100
But they’re not perfect – you might not get your head round the grammar and will lack the peer support you could get in a classroom environment.
但它们并非完美无缺——你可能无法理解语法知识，而且会缺少在课堂环境中能获得的同伴支持。

12
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:40,670
So, does technology spell the end of traditional classrooms and teachers?
那么，技术是否意味着传统课堂和教师的终结呢？

13
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:46,430
Guy Baron, head of modern languages at Aberystwyth University, thinks not.
阿伯里斯特威斯大学现代语言学院院长盖伊·巴伦并不这么认为。

14
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:54,840
He told the BBC that apps should be used alongside classroom methods, not to the exclusion of traditional teaching.
他向英国广播公司表示，应用程序应与课堂教学方法结合使用，而不是排斥传统教学。

15
00:01:54,840 --> 00:02:04,830
And he adds: "The apps are very conversational... they're not designed for degrees, but they could be additional resources."
他还补充道：“这些应用程序非常注重对话交流……它们并非为学位课程设计，但可以作为额外的学习资源。”

16
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:09,960
Certainly technology is going to help in and outside the classroom.
技术无疑会在课堂内外提供帮助。

17
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:16,960
But attending a real lesson, facing a real teacher, probably forces you to be more committed.
但参加真实的课程，面对真实的老师，可能会迫使你更加投入。

18
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:20,890
Motivation can be a problem when using an app.
使用应用程序学习时，动力可能是一个问题。

19
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:27,840
But if you have a genuine and practical reason to learn another language, you will no doubt stick with it.
但如果你有真实和现实的理由去学习另一门语言，你无疑会坚持下去。
